                <mxCell id="49" value="&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;This function behaves associative-ly, i.e.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;div&gt;release_area(A) + release_area(B) = release_area(B) + release_area(A)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;In case of composition of multiple release areas, i.e.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;release_area(A+B) = release_area(A) + release_area(B)&lt;br&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;the maximum of the initial conditions will be chosen,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;h = max(h_A, h_B)&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;strokeColor=none;dashed=1;dashPattern=12 12;" parent="1" vertex="1">
