                <mxCell id="75" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;High-Level structure of FASolverAvalanche.jl&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="462" width="365" height="70" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="76" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Note:&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt; The code is tailored for avalanche simulations. It doesn&#39;t support full user-defined workflows (like OpenFOAM), but allows custom rheology via user-supplied Julia functions.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt; Written in a C-style due to the developer’s embedded systems background. This enabled certain optimizations (e.g., runtime lookup tables), though it may deviate from typical Julia style.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt; Solver uses simple interpolation and time-stepping methods, prioritizing compatibility over high-accuracy results.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Fully compatible with &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-end=&quot;632&quot; data-start=&quot;616&quot;&gt;ForwardDiff.jl&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;; the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-end=&quot;644&quot; data-start=&quot;638&quot;&gt;Cell&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; structure supports &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-end=&quot;679&quot; data-start=&quot;664&quot;&gt;Float16/32/64&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-end=&quot;690&quot; data-start=&quot;684&quot;&gt;Dual&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt; types, assuming consistent floating-point type usage throughout.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="20" y="950" width="760" height="210" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>
